"schema": "nfl2k5_rookie_faces_templates/v1",
"note": "b779-rf3: the class generator's 68 templates (secondary records, four per position: high v0, high v1, low v0, low v1), rating bytes only (style channels kicking_style, power_run_style and scramble are left as the roster has them). Fitted so each position's drafted prospects match the real 2026 rookies as the SOFTDRINK v0.7 roster rates them, rating by rating (mean shift and spread scale; K, P, FB and FS use every team player with years pro <= 2 because fewer than 8 of them were drafted in 2026). The owner, 10/28: 'All prospects should have ratings similar to what makes the game play the best.' Applied by the rookie-faces build step after every other roster writer (the QB Throw Power curve included), so the values are final. b81 league-aging (coordinator 11/25): refitted for the grade roll (one grade per prospect, w 0.35) so each position's best generated rookies match the real 2026 class at the rookie season (rank-matched quantiles 0.5 and 0.9; the 0.9 at the 2026 CPU starters' mean minus 5, draft day to rookie season offsets measured under these rules (mean and top separately)); the low and high templates of a position move by one shift each; K, P and FB unchanged. Merged with b81 rookie-faces (11/26): the class generator's roll became one grade g per prospect and g + 0.25 (u - g) per rating (no clamp, no blue-chip draw: the rare-face pick took region C's spare bytes); every low/high rating pair above is widened by a third about its midpoint (as far as 0 and 99 allow), which reproduces the earlier roll's class (g + 0.35 (u - 0.5) on the pairs before widening) apart from its clamp and blue-chips.",
